# Mobile First

## Philosophy

Primary users discover via Instagram/WhatsApp, edit and view on phones. Desktop adapts from mobile, not the reverse.

## Targets

Optimize for low-end Android, mid-range Android, iPhone, tablets — small screens, slow networks, limited performance.

## Layout

- Start single-column, stacked sections, vertical scroll, touch-friendly spacing
- Fluid layouts; no fixed widths, horizontal overflow, or desktop-first grids on mobile

## Touch

- Minimum touch target: **44×44px**
- Easy to tap, clearly visible, properly spaced
- No hover-only functionality

## Navigation

Simple, thumb-friendly: bottom actions, collapsible menus. Avoid deep nested sidebars on mobile.

## Typography

Body 14–16px minimum; generous line-height; readable on small screens.

## Forms

Proper `inputMode`/keyboard types, autofill, large inputs. No multi-column forms on mobile.

## Scroll

Native smooth scroll only — no scroll-jacking, excessive sticky elements, or nested scroll containers.

## Performance

Lazy-load media; reduce JS and animations on mobile; test on real devices, not only browser resize.

## Dashboard & Editor

Collapsible panels, stacked layouts, bottom actions. Editor: instant preview updates; no tiny controls.

## Public Invitations

Fast load from WhatsApp links; immersive but readable; guest experience is critical.

## Priority

1. usability 2. touch 3. performance 4. readability 5. smooth interaction
